Before UI work, read `.impeccable.md` and, when available, `C:\Users\willi\.codex\design.md`.

Apply these guardrails automatically:

- Build the working product surface first.
- Keep parent-facing workflows calm, direct, and task-focused.
- Use existing components, tokens, routes, and patterns.
- Avoid generic AI UI patterns: gradient text, decorative orbs/blobs, glassmorphism, cards inside cards, fake metrics, repeated feature-card grids, and generic neon tech styling.
- Use icons for familiar actions.
- Design empty, loading, error, disabled, hover, focus, active, selected, long-text, mobile, and narrow-container states.
- Prevent text/control overlap and awkward overflow.
- Keep UX copy direct and specific.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences.

Do not edit `deliverables/` or `superpowers/` unless explicitly asked.
